WEBVTT

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:04.170
Hey, why the hell's Yabuki got bruises from head to toe?

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:08.910
S'not just Joe. His coach and his second are covered in 'em, too.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:35.840
How did Yabuki-kun get those bruises?

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.340
Does he really plan on fighting Wolf in that condition?

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:42.860
It's not the bruises I'm worried about.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:47.530
The reason for those bruises is far more ominous.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:52.560
To your corners.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.550
Fight!

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.950
Bring out your No Guard!

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:01.130
N-Now this... This is a shock!

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.640
Yabuki has raised a high guard!

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.600
He won't be using his usual No Guard stance on Wolf!

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.200
Tanaka-san, what do you make of this?

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:16.080
Well, I think it's the only natural course of action for Yabuki's camp.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.610
Natural? Why do you say that?

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.610
From what I've heard, Wolf's secret training...

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:25.940
was tailored to counter the Cross Counter, a punch Yabuki-kun throws from the No Guard position.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:29.620
So, if Yabuki were to use the No Guard stance in spite of that fact,

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.520
he'd be playing right into Wolf's hands.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:32.660
I see.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:36.330
It's been almost a minute since the bell rang,

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.480
but neither fighter has even thrown a jab!

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.810
Yabuki's in the center of the ring,

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:43.140
and Wolf has begun pacing around him, observing him carefully.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.640
It seems like Wolf is being extra-cautious.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:49.310
Well, I'd be pretty careful too if I were him.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:51.100
Not only is Yabuki covered in bruises,

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.600
but so are his coach, Tange, and his colleague, Mammoth Nishi.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.780
We can't explain those bruises.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:57.600
This is all incredibly strange.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:00.700
The standoff in the ring continues!

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.950
Hey! What are you doing, Ref!?

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.450
Quit standing there and do something!

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:13.340
Make them fight already, dammit!

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:15.640
We didn't pay to watch a staring competition!

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:20.250
Fight!

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.770
What's the matter, Wolf? You scared of Joe, or something?

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.140
You'd better get Daddy to help you!

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:45.400
Yabuki, you've played it cool for long enough now! Kick his ass already!{hm, just about?}

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:49.520
Yeah! Put Wolf out of his misery already!

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:53.180
You're pathetic, Wolf!

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.920
Wolf! Forget about his mind games! Just start punching!{added context}

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:06.930
I hear ya!

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.430
Wolf's started throwing punches!

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.180
He's throwing a barrage of jabs!

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.160
Yabuki's dodging them all the way to the ropes!

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.100
Yabuki's cornered on the ropes!

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.360
Wolf throws his first left hook of the match!

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:20.970
And what a scorcher that was!

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:24.820
Yabuki throws a right-left!

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.360
And it connects!

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:00.690
Back to your corners!

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.740
You're so cool, Joe!

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.650
Joe, you're so awesome!

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:35.560
Hey! Get a grip, Wolf!

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.350
Yabuki-kun has shown impressive progress in his technique.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:48.360
I never imagined I'd see him dodge jabs or do a swayback like that.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.000
Yes, he's definitely improving.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:54.730
But no matter how much he's improved, Wolf's still several rungs higher in the technique department.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:59.560
If this match keeps going the way it has been,

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:03.130
Wolf's bound to launch a counterattack eventually.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:18.680
Wolf, are you that worried about those bruises?

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:26.250
Don't sweat it, Wolf! I've figured out that those bruises are nothing to fear!

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:27.900
Think about it!

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:32.400
There are only three people at Tange Gym, if you include the coach!

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:36.980
Of course they'll be covered in bruises if they start training for real!

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:37.910
Ain't that right?

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:43.920
B-But, Coach, what about Joe's high guard?

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:45.990
That's not worth the time of day.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:49.920
He's just too afraid to drop his arms because he's scared of our secret training!

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.430
I-I get it!

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:20.120
Yabuki... You won't get it all your own way this round!

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:23.260
After all, I have the better technique and better career stats!

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:26.360
If you attack me head-on, I'll send you packing!

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:28.380
Besides, I have a trump card!

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:45.930
Wolf is down!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.950
Joe!

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:57.950
Bro Joe!

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:00.950
Way to go, Bro! Kick Wolf's ass!

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:03.450
You'd better goddamn stay down, Wolf!

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:05.460
Nice!

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.390
Joe's expressionless face...

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:34.490
And those two at the ringside haven't said a word today either.

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:36.490
There's something behind all this!

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:39.490
Get up, Wolf! Now's your chance, Wolf!

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.380
You did it!

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:42.930
Wolf's down for a second time!

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:45.530
Yabuki's mighty straight left connected!

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:47.810
Can Wolf get up from this?

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:49.390
Can he get up?

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:51.730
Get up, Wolf! Get up! You can't lose this!

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:54.160
You can't afford to lose this match!

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:55.900
Get up, Wolf!

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.320
Yeah, that's the way, Wolf!

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.440
You're gonna be the world champ!

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:02.980
The world's your oyster!

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:05.450
The world! The world!

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:10.410
The world?

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.970
Yes, the world...

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:13.920
This bastard...

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.520
is just a pebble I've stumbled over.

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:17.900
He's nothing, compared to me!

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:20.210
All I have to do is kick 
this pebble outta the way.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:23.280
And the way to do that...

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.490
is by beating his Cross Counter!

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:30.680
You won't fuck with me anymore, Yabuki!

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:32.180
Wolf! Look out!

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.190
I thought I told you, you won't fuck with me anymore!

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:56.410
Wolf!

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:03.390
Yabuki throws a right-left! Wolf throws a left-right! And it connects!

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:06.620
Yabuki's been pushed back into the corner!

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:08.130
Wolf throws a right-left!

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:10.060
Now, Yabuki throws a right!

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.930
What an intense exchange of blows! They're equal!

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:13.390
No, Wolf's coming out on top!

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:16.040
And that's it for the second round.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:19.400
Now, wasn't that an amazing exchange of blows?

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:21.140
Yes, it was impressive.

00:13:21.140 --> 00:13:24.260
But more importantly, that's Wolf's usual game right there.

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:27.910
He was overcome by Yabuki's strange aura in the first round and the first half of the second,

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:29.960
which made him stiffen up a bit.

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:32.870
But today's bout is about to get interesting!

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:39.250
Nicely done, Wolf. Keep it up.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.380
If you carry on like this, you'll gain the advantage!

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:43.400
Then, you can show him the results of your secret training!

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:44.620
The Anti-Cross Counter?

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:47.430
But Yabuki will have to use the No Guard for that...

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:49.070
I know that.

00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:52.930
But if you keep hurting him like that, he'll adopt the No Guard stance in no time.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.400
He'll have no other choice.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:56.440
I get you!

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:03.410
It looks like Wolf's about to launch his counterattack, Rikiishi-kun.

00:14:03.410 --> 00:14:08.180
We may even witness the results of Wolf's secret training next round.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.340
Wolf's secret training...

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:17.420
Yabuki, from what I hear, Wolf's secret training was the most intense in Asia Gym's history.

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:18.650
Which means...

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:44.040
Wolf hasn't just come up with a passive tactic to counter your Cross Counter...

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:46.590
He's mastered some form of killer blow.

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:51.200
And he's done it after extensively studying your Cross Counter!

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:58.720
Which means Wolf's waiting for you to bring out your No Guard so you can throw the Cross!

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:01.460
You understand, don't you, Yabuki?

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.430
<i>All right, that's the way!</i>

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:19.520
<i>Don't fall behind! This is Tange Gym's first special training session!</i>

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.750
<i>If this is too much for you, you'll never beat Wolf!</i>

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:34.910
Listen, Wolf. Do a thorough job!

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:33.720
<i>Wait!</i>

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.200
You did it, you did it, you did it!

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.740
That's the way, Wolf!

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:00.070
Yabuki's down!

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:02.780
Wolf's relentless rush has finally brought him down!

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:02.780
One!

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.030
Two!

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:07.170
Three!

00:17:07.800 --> 00:17:09.250
Bro!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:10.750
Joe!

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:13.760
Joe! Joe!

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:33.710
Four!

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:35.670
Five!

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:36.910
Six!

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.320
Seven!

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.960
Eight!

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:54.010
Yabuki, I hate to do this to you when you were finally doing so well...

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:56.840
But, think about it. The person you're facing is...

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:59.640
the precision machine, Wolf Kanagushi!

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:01.410
Now, what'll it be, Joe?

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:04.350
What're you gonna do now, <i>Joe-san</i>?

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:46.270
There it is! He's doing his floppy-arm stance!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:59.730
Joe! Isn't the No Guard playing right into Wolf's hands?

00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:03.280
What are you thinking, Joe?

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:04.830
What are you going to do?

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:23.850
You sure are stupid. This is just what I've been waiting for!

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:26.640
Now, it's time for me to entertain you!

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:06.320
Wolf!

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:11.260
Good enough. Do it.

00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:19.370
Yabuki. I promised I'd throw a straight left when I dropped by Tange Gym...

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:23.200
It's time to make good on my promise!

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:58.190
All right! You did it! You did it!

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:35.050
Y-Yabuki... Yabuki's the one who collapses!

00:21:35.050 --> 00:21:36.310
Yabuki's down!

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:52.350
I did it!

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:54.140
I did it, Coach!

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:58.290
I-It worked!

00:21:58.290 --> 00:22:00.460
Score!

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:02.060
Way to go!

00:22:02.060 --> 00:22:04.150
Hooray!

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:05.300
Hooray!!

00:22:05.300 --> 00:22:09.580
What just happened? I thought the Cross Counter connected!

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:11.810
Why did Yabuki collapse?

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:30.150
Th-The Anti-Cross Counter...

00:22:31.830 --> 00:22:33.490
Joe! Stand up!

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:35.620
Stand up, Joe!

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:36.830
Stand up!

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:08.990
Even though Joe trained and trained...

00:23:08.990 --> 00:23:11.990
The Cross Counter he threw with such confidence was eclipsed.

00:23:13.310 --> 00:23:16.910
As Wolf Kanagushi closes in for the kill with his fangs bared,

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:18.590
will Joe be defeated?

00:23:19.450 --> 00:23:23.580
You've done so much training for this match!

00:23:23.580 --> 00:23:25.950
Now, show us your progress!

00:23:26.590 --> 00:23:28.930
Lose the battle, but win the war!

00:23:28.930 --> 00:23:30.090
Now, stand up!

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:34.100
Tomorrow is coming soon!

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:36.510
If you win, then as a symbol of your victory,

00:23:36.510 --> 00:23:38.830
Rikiishi will surely stand before you in the ring!

00:23:38.830 --> 00:23:40.100
That's right!

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:42.110
Rikiishi Toru is not far ahead!

00:23:43.110 --> 00:23:44.770
Now, stand up!

00:23:44.770 --> 00:23:46.260
Stand tall until you win!

00:23:47.430 --> 00:23:49.110
On this square mat,

00:23:49.110 --> 00:23:53.610
show these boxing spectators your bloody victory!

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:56.370
You're the only one who can do it!

00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:58.120
You're the only one who can box like this!

00:23:59.480 --> 00:24:03.430
Now, for Joe, as he encounters the greatest crisis of his life so far,

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:05.090
which way is tomorrow!?
